{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Typetexp.TyVarEnv</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"melange","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Melange_compiler_libs","href":"../../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Typetexp","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"TyVarEnv","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-reset\"><a href=\"#val-reset\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">let</span> reset: <span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span> unit;</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>removes all type variables from scope</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-with_local_scope\"><a href=\"#val-with_local_scope\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">let</span> with_local_scope: <span><span>(<span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>)</span> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>;</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Evaluate in a narrowed type-variable scope</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-poly_univars\"><a href=\"#type-poly_univars\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> poly_univars</span><span>;</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-make_poly_univars\"><a href=\"#val-make_poly_univars\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">let</span> make_poly_univars: <span>list(string) <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span> <a href=\"#type-poly_univars\">poly_univars</a>;</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>remember that a list of strings connotes univars; this must always be paired with a <code>check_poly_univars</code>.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-check_poly_univars\"><a href=\"#val-check_poly_univars\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">let</span> check_poly_univars: \u000A  <span><a href=\"../../Env/index.html#type-t\">Env.t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><a href=\"../../Location/index.html#type-t\">Location.t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><a href=\"#type-poly_univars\">poly_univars</a> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span>\u000A  list(<a href=\"../../Types/index.html#type-type_expr\">Types.type_expr</a>);</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Verify that the given univars are universally quantified, and return the list of variables. The type in which the univars are used must be generalised</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-instance_poly_univars\"><a href=\"#val-instance_poly_univars\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">let</span> instance_poly_univars: \u000A  <span><a href=\"../../Env/index.html#type-t\">Env.t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><a href=\"../../Location/index.html#type-t\">Location.t</a> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span>\u000A  <span><a href=\"#type-poly_univars\">poly_univars</a> <span class=\"arrow\">=&gt;</span></span>\u000A  list(<a href=\"../../Types/index.html#type-type_expr\">Types.type_expr</a>);</span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p>Same as <code>check_poly_univars</code>, but instantiates the resulting type scheme (i.e. variables become Tvar rather than Tunivar)</p></div></div>"}